```
=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: switch0
diagnosis_text:
The fault is a Linux bridge (br0) on switch0 that was created and
populated with its two member interfaces but was never administratively
brought up. In a Kathara lab, software switches are implemented as Linux
bridges. switch0 bridges eth0 (uplink to router0 via link_r0_sw0) and
eth1 (downlink to the IT LAN, lan_it). Both physical ports are UP and
enslaved to br0, and STP is running on the bridge, but the bridge device
itself is stuck in DOWN state (kernel flags show <BROADCAST,MULTICAST>
with no UP or LOWER_UP bit set). Because the bridge is down the Linux
kernel refuses to forward any Layer-2 frames through it, so ARP requests
from IT hosts (192.168.1.x) never reach router0's eth0 (192.168.1.1),
and replies from router0 never reach the hosts. The result is the
observed "Destination Host Unreachable" from every IT host when trying
to reach the gateway. CS Department traffic flows through switch1, whose
br0 is correctly UP, which explains why CS is unaffected. The root
cause is a missing `ip link set br0 up` command in switch0's startup
configuration. The corrective fix is to add `ip link set br0 up` to
switch0's startup script (or execute it live: `ip link set br0 up` on
switch0), which will immediately restore Layer-2 connectivity between
router0 and the IT LAN.
=== END ===
```